Not remembering words is not a sign of non-fluency. It happens to native
speakers all the time. And to me, 'native' implies 'fluent'.

stevo

On Wed, Feb 15, 2012 at 5:00 PM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:

> I think even that happening once in a while is ok.  One of my co-workers
> is German who I would say is fluent in English but who every now and then
> will stop and have to ask "what is that word that means...".
>
> I think it's unreasonable to say that a person isn't fluent just because
> they don't know every word.
>
> I think commonness of the word has to come into play.  If a person
> struggles to remember the word "person" I'd say they're not fluent but a
> person who struggles to remember "aggregate" could definitely be "fluent".
>
>
